# PowerPredict

4th-year academic project: smart-building energy forecasting (BDG2, FastAPI, React, MQTT, SHAP). Prioritize correctness, reproducibility, explainability, and a runnable demo.

## Stack (do not substitute)

- Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Recharts
- Backend: Python, FastAPI, Pydantic; Postgres via `DATABASE_URL`
- ML: pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, XGBoost, PyTorch, SHAP
- IoT: MQTT (Mosquitto) + Python simulator
- Local Docker Compose for Postgres + Mosquitto only

## Do not introduce

Kubernetes, microservices, Redis-as-a-platform, reinforcement learning, digital twins, transformers as the main model, extra cloud SaaS, or WebSockets (IoT UI polls).

## Correctness

- Never fabricate metrics, forecasts, or experimental results.
- Never shuffle time-series data.
- Label simulated occupancy and simulated IoT as simulated in data, API, and UI.
- Training is an offline CLI; the API loads saved artifacts only.

## Security (minimum)

JWT from env secrets, explicit CORS origins (no `*`), rate limits with 429 + quota headers. No hardcoded credentials.
